    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Kyle Tucker** (72.21), our premier play against Michael King. **Tucker** benefits from a strong SP skill matchup and an advantageous spot in the lineup, making him our most reliable source of production. He is joined at the top of the board by **Drake Baldwin** (70.07), who finds himself in an enviable position against a soft matchup versus Williamson. **Baldwin**\u2019s elite scoring is fueled by an excellent SP skill rating (+19%) and a premium #2 hole placement, making him the anchor of our lineup efficiency today. **Miguel Vargas** also commands attention (62.40) as our leadoff hitter; his xwOBA of 0.381 combined with a favorable matchup against Lynch IV provides a high-floor opportunity to accumulate counting stats early.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Brayan Rocchio** (36.10), who fell just shy of the 40-point efficiency floor. While his park factors were positive, the combination of a tough outing against Tolle and a bottom-of-the-order assignment (-8%) pushed him out of the active set. Meanwhile, we are managing a few risks: **Jackson Merrill** (58.27) is a strong play assuming he hits #5, though his status remains \"Lineup Pending,\" and **Heliot Ramos** (44.06) faces headwinds from an unfavorable wind forecast at the park. We are also navigating the absence of **Gunnar Henderson** due to a postponement, which forces us to rely on our active depth to keep pace in the Roto standings. We remain thin in the infield with **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** currently sidelined on the IL, placing additional pressure on **Josh Jung** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to provide stable production in the middle infield and at the hot corner.",
